counterexample:
No counterexample to (a) to (d). Counterexample to the "hence" inference in (e), checked with numpy: at (m,n,r) = (4,5,2), HF orthogonal init gives dim S1 = 1·(9−1) = 8 = mr = dim S1(T_A). The deficits are equal (6 = 6) and the images are identical (θ0 + M_{≤2}). The same happens at (6,8,4), where both have dim S1 = 24. So apex status plus dim S1 do not show the class is new. Numerically, the S1 subspaces still differ: S1(orth) contains u wᵀ for u ∈ col B0 ≠ 0 and arbitrary w, which is not in {Z : row Z ⊆ row A0}. Also confirmed numerically:
- dims (14, 10, 20, 11) at (7,5,2);
- S1(T_A) ≠ S1(T_B) at m = n = 5;
- dim S1 matches m·rk A + n·rk B − rk A·rk B in all cases tested;
- the annihilator of S1 has dimension (m − rk B)(n − rk A), with column/row spans recovering (col B0)^⊥ and (row A0)^⊥.

